ref_dict.th-v:
\begin{theorem}
\label{th-v}
There is an absolute positive constant $C$ such that for each pair $m,N$ with 
$4\le m \le (\log N)^2$ the number of $n\le N$ with $m/n$ not the sum of $3$
unit fractions is at most $N/\exp(C(\log^2(N)/\varphi(m))^{1/3})$.
\end{theorem}

