via dynamic rescaling, thereby transforming the singularity formation problem into the stability analysis of an approximate steady state in the rescaled variables”; (ii) “we perform the stability analysis of this approximate steady state in the rescaled formulation,” which involves “the identification of an approximate steady state” and “energy estimates in a singularly weighted norm, providing both linear and nonlinear stability of this approximate profile”; then, “by tracing back to the original variables, this yields finite time blow-up for the inviscid model (the equation above)”; (iii) “we establish convergence of the dynamically rescaled solution to the true self-similar profile.” The organization paragraph adds that next they present “the construction of a family of self-similar profiles for (the equation above) when $a$ is close to 1, together with their stability analysis and the proof of the main theorem.”

